  chousa-shokunin/corpus/QUALITY.md:1046:143. **An outer battery prints no invertible answer key, no strippable subject identity and no receipt a child can append to; its predicate is bound to the exit code.** Round 77's battery printed `sha256` of the permuted subject names, and a critic recovered both per-run permutations by enumerating 13! inside the battery's own 300 s cap (11.8 s and 59.1 s, `R77CriticA/rcpt-a7.txt`), then reached the exact predicate line with exit 0 without scoring a subject; the salt is an appended suffix, so a content hash classified every subject (`rcpt-a1.txt`), and `/proc/<ppid>/cmdline` handed the matrix the `CONTRACT` cells (`rcpt-a2.txt`). A detached helper also appended 26 copies of the predicate line after the battery exited 1 (`rcpt-a5d.txt`). Check before a successor freeze: the printed digest is of the seed, not of the permutation; the salted copy is rewritten rather than suffixed; the contract cells are derived per run, not read from the judge's source; and the predicate is read together with the exit code the receipt records. Shown able to fail: the three cited receipts reach the frozen line at exit 0 and the fourth forges a receipt whose exit is 1. — `lessons/round-77.md`, Instrument limits.
